---
import DistaDocs from "../../../../components/DistaDocs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { DISTA_REPO, distaDocs } from "../../../../data/dista";

const description =
  "How to use Dista: installing it and a first program, then tasks and results, shuffles, actors, running a cluster, the dista command, failure and recovery, and tuning, each on a page of its own.";

const about: Record<string, string> = {
  "/s/dista/docs/tasks":
    "Declaring tasks, where results live and how they're freed, tasks on other tasks' results, cancelling and timeouts, and what crosses the wire.",
  "/s/dista/docs/shuffles":
    "Tasks with several results, tasks taking a value beside results, placement by data location, and spilling.",
  "/s/dista/docs/actors":
    "State on a worker of its own, handles passed to tasks, restarts, checkpoints, and actors moving off a draining worker.",
  "/s/dista/docs/cluster":
    "Roles from the environment, the generic head, Kubernetes and EC2, draining a worker, and autoscaling.",
  "/s/dista/docs/cli":
    "dista head, status, drain, scale, timeline and stop; Prometheus metrics; the task timeline.",
  "/s/dista/docs/failures":
    "What happens when a task raises, a worker dies or goes silent, a task hangs, a driver leaves, or the head restarts.",
  "/s/dista/docs/tuning":
    "Tasks in flight per worker, backpressure, the node store and spilling, memory held for drivers, and large results.",
};
---

<DistaDocs href="/s/dista/docs" description={description}>
  <p class="eyebrow">Docs</p>
  <h1 class="section-title">Using Dista</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Dista turns ordinary Mojo functions into tasks that run across a cluster. One binary
    runs as the driver, the head and every worker, on a laptop or on Kubernetes. This page
    installs it and runs a first program; the pages below cover the rest. How it works is
    in the repository's <a href={`${DISTA_REPO}/blob/main/DESIGN.md`} rel="noopener">DESIGN.md</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="pages">The docs</h2>
  <ul class="docs-list">
    {distaDocs.slice(1).map((d) => (
      <li><a href={d.href}><strong>{d.title}</strong></a>: {about[d.href]}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2 id="install">Install it</h2>
  <p>
    Dista is the mojoshelf tin <code>dista-mojo</code>, version 0.2.2. With pixi and
    mojoshelf's <code>pixi shelf</code> installed, a new project adds it, and the tins it
    needs (arrow-mlake, memory-region and objectstore) come with it:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock label="shell" code={`pixi init -c https://conda.modular.com/max-nightly -c conda-forge app && cd app
sed -i.bak 's/^\\[workspace\\]/[workspace]\\npreview = ["pixi-build"]/' pixi.toml   # tins build with pixi-build
pixi add "mojo-compiler==1.2.0"
pixi shelf add dista-mojo`} />
  <p>
    It targets Mojo 1.2.0, and its CI also runs on the 1.3 nightly. Reading Parquet and
    Iceberg tables in tasks uses magmalake's <code>parquet-mojo</code> and
    <code>iceberg-mojo</code> beside it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="first">A first program</h2>
  <p>
    A task is a top-level <code>def</code>, declared once with its argument and result
    types, and registered in the runtime's parameter list:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock label="Mojo" code={`from dista import ObjectRef, Runtime, Task

def square(x: Int) -> Int:
    return x * x

comptime Square = Task[Int, Int, square]

def main() raises:
    var rt = Runtime[Square](workers=4)
    var refs = List[ObjectRef[Int]]()
    for i in range(1000):
        refs.append(rt.remote[Square](i))
    var total = 0
    for r in refs:
        total += rt.take(r)  # get and release: read once, then freed
    print(total)  # 332833500`} />
  <p>
    Build it with <code>mojo build</code> and run it. With nothing set in its environment,
    it forks a head and four workers on this machine and drives them. Point the same
    binary at a head and it joins a cluster instead:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock label="shell" code={`DISTA_ROLE=head DISTA_PORT=6390 ./app                  # the head
DISTA_ROLE=worker DISTA_HEAD=headhost:6390 ./app       # once per worker
DISTA_HEAD=headhost:6390 ./app                         # the driver`} />
  <p>
    <a href="/s/dista/docs/tasks">Tasks and results</a> says what a task can take and
    return, and <a href="/s/dista/docs/cluster">Running a cluster</a> how the roles fit
    together.
  </p>

  <h2 id="source">From source</h2>
  <p>
    The repository builds and tests with pixi. <code>pixi run cli</code> builds the
    <code>dista</code> command to <code>build/dista</code>.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock label="shell" code={`git clone ${DISTA_REPO} && cd dista.mojo
pixi run test               # codec, frame, runtime and cluster tests, Mojo 1.2.0
pixi run -e nightly test    # the same on the 1.3 nightly
pixi run -e data test-data  # tasks over Parquet and Iceberg; needs those tins checked out next door
pixi run bench              # task throughput
pixi run test-kind          # the smoke test on a kind cluster (needs docker, kind, kubectl)`} />
  <p>
    What each release changed is in
    <a href={`${DISTA_REPO}/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md`} rel="noopener">CHANGELOG.md</a>, and
    what Dista is for, with its phases, in
    <a href={`${DISTA_REPO}/blob/main/VISION.md`} rel="noopener">VISION.md</a>.
  </p>
</DistaDocs>

<script is:inline>
  // This page used to hold every section. Old links go to the section's new page.
  (function () {
    var to = {
      tasks: "tasks#tasks", results: "tasks#results", graphs: "tasks#graphs",
      types: "tasks#types",
      shuffles: "shuffles",
      actors: "actors", checkpoints: "actors#checkpoints",
      running: "cluster",
      watching: "cli", timeline: "cli#timeline",
      failures: "failures",
    };
    var h = location.hash.slice(1);
    if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(to, h)) location.replace("/s/dista/docs/" + to[h]);
  })();
</script>
